Day 7 – Process & System monitoring

# What I Learned
  - how to monitor system processes
# Commands Practiced
  - ps 
  - ps aux
  - ps aux | grep *particular process name*
  - top
  - htop (a better version)
  - kill PID
  - kill -9 PID for stubborn ones
# What I Understood in Simple Words
  - ps aux to see all running programs
  - ps aux | grep to search a process and get their PID
  - we can use that PID to kill the process
  - top and htop for live system monitering
